    "body": "## Current scope and status\n\nMora authorized implementation on 2026-10-05. The adopted design and authorization are recorded in [DECISIONS.md](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/blob/claude/pensive-meitner-wrg9b0/nix/sandhi/docs/DECISIONS.md) at b6b25bd.\n\nThis draft now implements Stage A: a standalone Python endpoint with mutual TLS, certificate-to-installation mapping, bounded messages, durable inbox/outbox state, restart recovery, a replaceable deterministic responder, Nix packaging, and a three-guest NixOS experiment. The exchange itself uses direct TLS connections and local state, with no GitHub relay or human message forwarding.\n\nStage A tests transport using a split-input computation. It does not yet run AI models. The production Sandhi modules and existing six-check validation scope remain unchanged; the VM experiment is separate.\n\n## Verified and pending\n\n- Tessera verified source **29c7303**: **58 Sandhi Python tests passed**, including two-process mutual-TLS exchanges and restart cases; **15 archive tests passed**; `anchor.py verify` passed for 10 records.\n- Recovery/deadline fixes in 29c7303 address interrupted terminal commits, interrupted conversation binding, expired outgoing messages, and responder execution beyond the deadline.\n- Sideband recorded VM attempts 1 and 2 as setup failures, with fixes committed. Attempt 3 was reported running against a5dbe45; its result cannot validate the newer recovery patch.\n- **Pending:** a recorded VM run including 29c7303 or a descendant, followed by review of all eleven assertions and evidence. No complete Stage A VM pass is claimed here.\n- Model adapters, exchanges between model families, and deployments under independent administration remain subsequent stages.\n\nCoordination and the latest implementation handoff: https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/pull/6#issuecomment-5998565167\n\n## Original proposal description (historical)\n\nThe text below predates Mora's authorization and the implementation. Its docs-only status is superseded by the current status above.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Sideband's original proposal description</summary>\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds `nix/sandhi/docs/PROPOSAL-STANDALONE-EXCHANGE.md`, a discussion document for the question: can two independently installed copies of Sandhi carry a conversation between AI agents from different model families, with no GitHub dependency and no person relaying messages?\n\n- Records the shared finding (Tessera and this Claude session): the current package has no communication endpoint, model adapter, peer authentication, conversation state or message-evidence integration.\n- Lists constraints read from the code that shape a design: ingress filtering, no low ports, finite `runtimeMaxSec`, public contract values, IPv4 literals, and the experiment-0 DNS path.\n- Proposes four stages: (A) deterministic transport, (B) local open-weight models, (C) hosted adapters, which need Mora's decision, and (D) separate operators.\n- Ends with open questions for Tessera and Mora.\n\nThis PR is the thread for that dialogue. It is not a decision; accepted scope goes into DECISIONS.md before any code. No modules, tests, workflows or archive objects change.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `python3 anchor.py verify` passes. Docs-only, so the Sandhi workflow is not triggered by design.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015s6RDyrZi18RQbAB2cUffu\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_015s6RDyrZi18RQbAB2cUffu)_\n\n</details>\n",
